Answer: Inheritance is implemented using the extends keyword. Example:

```java
class Student extends Human {
}
```

Here: Human → Parent class Student → Child class The Student class inherits properties and behaviors from Human.

Answer: Suppose name, age, and gender are defined inside Human. Without inheritance, Student cannot directly use those properties because they are not defined in Student. When the following relationship is created:

```java
class Student extends Human {
}
```

the properties and behaviors of Human become available to Student. Therefore, Student can use: name age gender eat() along with its own properties and behavior.

