Here: Human → Parent Student → Child extends → Establishes inheritance The child class can use the properties and behaviors available from the parent class.

Answer: Inheritance establishes a parent-child relationship between classes. Parent Class ↓ Properties + Behaviors ↓ Child Class The child class can acquire properties and behaviors from the parent class. The Java keyword used to establish this relationship is: extends Example:

```java
class Student extends Human {
}
```

This allows the Student class to use its own properties and behaviors together with the properties and behaviors inherited from Human.
